} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "11 – 13 August 1932"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/305"} "Olympic Park Swimming Stadium, Los Angeles, California"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/4999"} "14 from 9 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Already the winner of two gold medals at the Games, " [:a {:href "/athletes/51105"} "Helene Madison"] " was the world record holder at this event. When the reigning Olympic silver medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/49375"} "Zus Philipsen-Braun"] " was forced to withdraw from competition, Madison’s victory seemed to be assured."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final turned out to be far closer than anybody anticipated and on a par with the " [:a {:href "/results/4946"} "men’s event"] " at the same games. For the majority of the race, Madison and her teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/51082"} "Lenore Kight"] " swam in procession, with Madison always holding a slender lead. However, with 100 metres to go, Kight made her move and overtook Madison. Madison responded to Kight’s efforts and the two women battled down their final length of the pool. Madison timed her finish well and touched the wall ahead of Kight, the clock showing a tenth of a second dividing the two Americans, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/49983"} "Jenny Maakal"] " of South Africa a full twenty seconds further back.  Kight had a poor turning technique which may have contributed to her defeat."] "\n\n" [:p {} "This was the final race of Madison’s brief career. She celebrated her victory at a party attended by Hollywood celebrities, and she would even dance with Clark Gable. The circumstances of Zus Philipsen-Braun’s withdrawal due to illness are shrouded in mystery. By the time of the final, the Dutchwoman was in hospital and seriously ill with blood poisoning after an infection officially caused by a mosquito bite. However, Philipsen-Braun herself was convinced she was the victim of a deliberate attempt to remove her from contention as part of a possible betting coup."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51105"} "Helene Madison"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "5:44.5 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "5:48.7 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "5:28.5 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51082"} "Lenore Kight"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "5:40.9 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "5:50.8 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "5:28.6 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/49983"} "Jenny Maakal"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RSA.png"}] "RSA"]] [:td {} "5:53.9 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "6:00.6 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "5:47.3 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46996"} "Joyce Cooper"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "5:56.7 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "6:00.4 (3 h2)"] [:td {} "5:49.7 (4)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46725"} "Yvonne Godard"]] [:td {} [:a {:hre